# media/windows/sidebar-hold.cmds — the sidebar's rows hold still while the pointer is over them (so a
# row doesn't slide away under the next click), and let go when it leaves. On Windows nothing tells
# GPUI that a pointer went off the window's edge: 0.4.1-beta.1 went on holding (and left the last
# thing hovered lit, its tooltip up), and a thread started meanwhile never showed in the list until
# the pointer came back and crossed it. `realleave` is Windows saying the pointer left (the machine's
# cursor isn't one a script can move: the window is told where it is). Windows only.
# Run: pwsh script/capture.ps1 windows/sidebar-hold

pace 0
theme night
glass off
project @REPO@
send first
wait idle 30000
route draft
count live-line-0* 1

# As the beta had it: the pointer is on the sidebar, a thread starts elsewhere, its row waits...
legacy-pointer on
realmove open-notes
send second
wait idle 30000
count live-line-0* 1
shot hold-beta-held
# ...the pointer goes off the window's edge, and it waits still, Notes still lit with its tooltip.
realleave
wait 600
count live-line-0* 1
shot hold-beta-gone

# Now: the same pointer, off the window's edge, lets the list catch up and takes the light off Notes.
legacy-pointer off
realmove open-notes
realleave
wait 600
count live-line-0* 2
shot hold-gone
